  `persist ms` is how long a repeat of the same kick still produces the
  same population pattern; `reliab r` is that correlation in the first
  bin; `changes r` compares the first bin's pattern with the last
  reliable one — near 1 is a frozen attractor holding still, which is a
  memory rather than a sequence.

  THERE IS A REGIME — the kick survives 168 ms with the pattern still
  reproducible and still changing. This kernel can carry a sequence;
  what it lacks is something that USES one.
