  travelsweep REFUSED -- THE DEMAND DOES NOT REACH THE LEARNER, so this
  ladder cannot measure a travel ceiling. Past the point where the creature
  stops crossing its target, moving the target further adds a CONSTANT to
  the formant error, and the caregiver's bar is an EMA of that same error --
  the constant cancels and the reward sequence is bit-identical. The
  creature is not refusing to travel further; it is never asked to.

  THAT IS THE RESULT, and it is a bigger one than the curve would have
  been: the naming ceiling has a cause in the TEACHING PROTOCOL rather
  than in the larynx. Read the rungs that DO differ for how far the voice
  gets while the demand is still visible, and see `baseref` -- a bar that
  tracks the creature stops asking. The next question is whether an
  ABSOLUTE component in the bar makes the distance visible again, or
  whether it simply removes the praise variance that makes any learning
  possible at all.
