  differ; +7.2 SE over its own control). Delivered separation is +0.1646
  against the shipped rule's +0.2710, a difference of -0.1064. READ THE
  |R| AND praise COLUMNS BEFORE CALLING THIS A FIX: if this arm's mean
  |reward| is far from the shipped arm's, part of the difference is a
  learning rate and not a bar.

  abshard: THE BAR IS NEVER CROSSED -- `baseref` CONFIRMED IN ITS
  SHARPEST FORM. The distance reaches the learner (31/36 seeds differ),
  and the reward stops varying: sd(R) 0.0334 against the shipped rule's
  0.4967, praise fraction in the table above. A fixed bar placed where
  the shipped rule SETTLES is a bar the creature has not reached YET,
  so every trial gets the same sign, drift is zero, and it never will.
  The tracking bar works precisely because it follows the creature up
  from wherever it starts. A bar that tracks stops asking; a bar that
  does not stops being answered, and this is the second half measured.
