  DNA v63 PRE-FLIGHT -- would a BURST-weighted centroid differentiate
  the group further than a RATE-weighted one? Computed from the burst
  profile as measured; no readout is built to ask this.
    arm           rate centroid  burst centroid burst Hz     creatures
    burst         0.3912 +/- 0.0075 0.5963 +/- 0.0154 0.4597 +/- 0.0121 12
    burst-quiet   0.5002 +/- 0.0001 0.4865 +/- 0.0081 0.5132 +/- 0.0182 12

    SIGNED deflection from 0.5:  rate -0.1088   burst +0.0963
    naming needs 0.153 (230 Hz of separation on a 750 Hz lerp)

    THE SIGNS ARE OPPOSED, which is the finding. rate - burst would
    ADD the deflections: 0.2052, or 1.34x the 0.153 naming needs.
    DO NOT BUILD ON THAT YET: these are BETWEEN-creature SEs, and burst
    events run 0.44 Hz against ~4.5 Hz of spikes. A sparse centroid's
    PER-FRAME noise is the same trade that refused the two-pool readout
    and it must be measured on the covariance before anything is built.

    REFUSED -- the burst profile is no less flat than the rate profile
    (0.0963 vs -0.1088). Homeostasis is not what limits differentiation, or
    bursts inherit the flatness rather than escaping it. Either way the
    opening this pre-flight was built on is not there.

