  --- the verdict ---
  THE ASYMMETRY FOLLOWS THE TARGET. (bot7-top7) is +8.9 SE at the low
  target and -8.7 SE at the high one -- the same two blocks, opposite
  signs. Nothing is special about the upper cells: the lesson recruits
  whichever half can move the centroid the way it is being asked to.
  SO WRITE SEPARATION HAS A ROUTE THAT NEEDS NO MASK. Two lessons with
  targets on OPPOSITE sides of rest recruit DIFFERENT halves. That is the
  F1-internal version of `capacity`'s orthogonal case, and it is the first
  time this chapter has pointed at something buildable rather than at a
  readout to redesign.

  READ THE PROFILE ABOVE WHATEVER THE COSTS DID: which half moves, and in
  which direction, is the mechanism and it does not depend on the gate.
