  --- the verdict ---
  IT IS THE COMPONENT ALONG A's OWN AXIS. Same distance in the other axis
  costs A nothing (+0.1 SE against `keep`), the same distance in A's axis
  destroys it (+14.4 SE apart), and piling a large F2 demand on top of a
  fixed F1 demand changes nothing (+1.3 SE).
  ONE ACCOUNT NOW COVERS `retain`'s 0.22 AND `capacity`'s 0.84: they are the
  same creature measured at two angles, not two phenomena.
  AND IT IS BUILDABLE: a second lesson is retainable if its target does not
  require A's axis to move -- a property of the TARGET PAIR, arranged for
  free. The limit is equally clear: within ONE formant there is only one
  axis, so two F1 lessons can never be made orthogonal this way.

  THE RATE COLUMN IS THE MECHANISM CHECK: `gapwrite` says losing A looks like
  A's suppressed neurons being restored, so gap dUPPER should track retention
  across the arms. That was predicted here, not fitted to what came back.
