  --- the verdict ---
  A LESSON SILENT ABOUT A's AXIS IS FREE. `f2-axis` retains 0.930 against
  `f1-axis`'s 0.272 (+5.2 SE), and A comes out of the gap no worse than it
  went in. The second lesson was rewarded the whole time -- on F2 alone --
  so this is not an idle gap.
  THAT COMPLETES THE ACCOUNT: `retain`'s wipe and `capacity`'s coexistence
  are one mechanism seen at two angles, and whether a second lesson costs the
  first is a property of WHAT IT ASKS, not of how far away it is.
  THE LIMIT IS UNCHANGED AND SHOULD BE SAID IN THE SAME BREATH: within ONE
  formant there is one axis, so two F1 lessons can never be made orthogonal
  this way. This buys coexistence ACROSS articulators, not within one.
