  A HYPOTHESIS, NOT A FINDING. F2 looks more steerable by 2.9 SE, which is
  inside the 2-3 SE band this project has retracted three findings from. The
  effect is +0.079 of the demanded move, about 25% relative -- REAL if it
  holds, but nothing should be built on it until it is confirmed at more
  seeds (~67 for 4 SE).
  WHAT IS SOLID REGARDLESS: both axes respond strongly to reward (22.9 and
  21.7 SE over their own untaught controls), and the axis gap is ~25%
  rather than the 5.6x `orthovocab` appeared to show. So the bulk of that
  run's 0.169-against-0.030 WAS the collision, and a lesson fighting another
  on its own axis simply cannot travel.
