  NO SHARED TIME COURSE — only 5.2% of an utterance's movement is
  shared with the other utterances. They vary, but each varies its own
  way: there is variability and no sequence. A setpoint plus noise is
  all this larynx produces, which is what a scalar
  `drive_compensation` in place of HVC predicts. Reward cannot select
  a trajectory that is never repeated, so a word is unreachable until
  something generates one.

